{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460273-v5-i-ve-made-an-advanced-discord-dicebot-for-v5-games","id":1460273,"title":"[V5] I've made an advanced Discord dicebot for V5 games","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-17T17:59:23-07:00","id":1460273,"title":"[V5] I've made an advanced Discord dicebot for V5 games","content":"Apologies if this isn't allowed here.<br /> <br /> I've released Inconnu, an advanced V5 Discord dicebot. In addition to basic pool/hunger/difficulty rolls, you can also input your character's skills and attributes (and define your own traits) and use <i>them</i> in a roll. So instead of &quot;roll 7 dice&quot;, you can go &quot;roll strength + brawl&quot;. Inconnu also lets you store macros (predefined rolls that use hunger and have a default difficulty), manage your health/wp/humanity/hunger/stains/etc., and a whole bunch of other stuff.<br /> <br /> Full documentation, including bot invite link, is here: <a href=\"https://www.inconnu-bot.com/#/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.inconnu-bot.com/#/</a><br /> Demo server is here: <a href=\"https://discord.gg/CPmsdWHUcZ\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/CPmsdWHUcZ</a><br /> <br /> Inconnu is 100% free to use and open source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://github.com/tiltowait/inconnu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://github.com/tiltowait/inconnu\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://github.com/tiltowait/inconnu\" target=\"_blank\"> https://github.com/tiltowait/inconnu </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26481-tiltowait","name":"tiltowait","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T02:41:17-07:00","id":1460313,"title":"","content":"Ooh, cool stuff. I run a Masquerade chronicle over Discord and I'm always interested in bots that can enhance the experience.<br /> <br /> If you use a &quot;roll Strength + Brawl&quot; command, do people see the number of dice rolled in the pool? I prefer to keep PCs' character sheets secret from everyone besides their player, but I've not found any bots that keep dice pools hidden.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T17:03:36-07:00","id":1460391,"title":"","content":"It does show the full size of the pool\u2014though if you rolled Strength + Brawl, it won\u2019t show the individual traits (i.e. they won\u2019t know you have strength 3 and brawl 2).<br /> <br /> One potential workaround: If you are a server admin, you can roll on behalf of other users. So you could roll for someone in a private dice-rolling channel. Not exactly what you want, but it\u2019s there. I do see the utility in hidden pools, and I\u2019ll consider ways to implement them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26481-tiltowait","name":"tiltowait","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-18T22:06:21-07:00","id":1460408,"title":"","content":"That would be a really cool feature. I am the server admin and could roll for my players, but I think they would (quite reasonably) prefer to roll their own dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T17:16:14-07:00","id":1460482,"title":"","content":"It's a tricky problem. While I think most players would enjoy having their own dice hidden, they enjoy the accountability that visible pools brings. Unfortunately, there's no way to make parts of messages visible only to certain roles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26481-tiltowait","name":"tiltowait","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}